This is an assessment component for the Cloud and Distributed Computing module worth 30%. 
 
Description 
You are asked to design and implement a (smart) (intelligent) (reliable) (secure) cloud-based distributed 
system. You will then write a report in the form of a research article documenting your design and 
implementation. The implemented system should demonstrate some original contribution that you will 
need to argue in your report by comparing and contrasting it to related research and/or industrial work. 
You are free to choose what will be the focus of your contribution. It can be a distributed (Gen)(AI) 
application utilising cloud computing and cloud native that introduce some novel functionality, for 
example, a distributed measurement system to give a network-wide view of performance; an integrated 
distributed system employing technologies ranging from cloud computing, artificial intelligence and 
embedded system; a distributed data collection and analytic framework for environmental monitoring. 
Your project MUST incorporate the cloud native framework such as container and/or Kubernetes, 
applying what you have learnt from the Dell’s online courses in this module. 
You will undertake this assignment in groups to accommodate for the extra load of research in deriving 
your own specification and design for the system you will be implementing. It is the group members’ 
responsibility to divide the work and manage the overall project. 
The following list contains a few past examples of what can constitute an original contribution but it is 
by no means exhaustive: 
• A smart distributed sensor-actuator application that offers intelligent automation in a home area 
network. 
• Implementation of a (new) consensus algorithm for a mini-Blockchain 
• Building a Raspberry Pi cloud (https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/6679872) 
(https://raspberrypicloud.wordpress.com/) 
• Porting an existing cloud-based distributed system to Google RPC (https://grpc.io) 
• Adding distribution and containerise some centralised/monolithic systems, implement microservice 
architecture 

