Progress Presentation (15%): This is a mid-point check on your project’s progress. Marks will be 
allocated based on the progress made. You will be given 5-10 mins of presentation time in the tutorial 
session and each group member is expected to explain his/her contribution. 
Implementation (25%): Marks will be awarded for working systems that implement the advertised 
functionality. Level of marks will depend on the originality and contribution of the system and the level 
of challenge involved in realising it. Inclusion of advanced features such as concurrency control, 
serverless architecture, server callbacks, etc. will also be taken into consideration. You are NOT 
expected to provide any sophisticated (G)UI for your system. Your solution should mainly focus on 
aspects of the system that make it functions in a cloud native and distributed fashion. 
Presentation (18%): Each group will be required to submit a short video of 10 to 15-minute in duration, 
describing their implementation, detailing the functionalities and the design justification of the 
distributed application they have developed. **The top 3 project teams will be invited to present 
their project to a panel of judges to be considered for the Dell Cloud Native Award. 
Article/Report (25%): Marks will be awarded for coherent articles that will satisfactorily address the 
main points of the relevant sections outlined above. Particular attention should be given to the 
construction of the argument regarding the originality of the implemented system and its comparison to 
related work, as well as to the quantitative evaluation of the system. 
 
*Note: Each member be required to submit a peer evaluation score to rate the other members’ 
contribution at the end of the project. The final mark will be adjusted based on the peer 
evaluation score. 
 
 
